{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgzBvowyD1U6j5Cx7Tf7C","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I can say what the variable does. I can't say why step 4 sets it, because that isn't written down anywhere.\n\n**What it does:** the docstring in `kiln/timeparse.py:3` says `KILN_LEGACY_TZ=1` makes `parse()` treat timestamps with no timezone as UTC, which is how kiln behaved before 2.0. Without it, the docstring says they're read as local time. The code doesn't actually do that: it leaves them with no timezone at all.\n\n**Why step 4 sets it:** unknown. SETUP.md gives no reason, and the variable has been in step 4 since the first commit, `d274cef Initial development setup`, so the history doesn't explain it either.\n\n**What I checked:** the test suite doesn't depend on it. All 3 tests pass without the variable, including with `TZ=America/New_York`. The only timezone test checks the hour of a timestamp with no timezone, and that comes out the same either way.\n\nSo it may well be a leftover, but passing tests don't prove that. Someone may have added it to keep the old UTC reading for timestamps in `fixtures/` or for local debugging, and none of the 3 tests would catch that. Since its purpose was never recorded, I haven't changed step 4. Should I remove it? Or if you know why it was there, I can write that reason next to it instead."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":377,"cache_read_input_tokens":21403,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":377},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<uuid-1>","uuid":"<uuid-36>","timestamp":"2026-11-13T03:07:10.361Z","request_id":"req_011CgzBvooHEpARHh5QgEk7s"}
